      ],
      "common_pitfall": "A missing tens place may need 零 (líng): 一百零五 (yì bǎi líng wǔ), not 一百五 when you specifically mean 105.",
      "pronunciation_focus": "Before a fourth-tone syllable, 一 (yī) normally sounds like yí; before a non-fourth tone, it often becomes yì. Displayed lexical pinyin may follow a different citation convention.",
